<% content_for :title, "Reporting and Legal Protection | SafeSpace Malaysia" %>

<div class="resource-page">
  <section class="resource-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="resource-eyebrow">MALAYSIA • KNOW YOUR OPTIONS</span>
      <h1 class="resource-title mt-3">Reporting &amp; legal protection</h1>
      <p class="resource-lead mt-3">
        If you are experiencing domestic violence, there are steps you can
        consider to seek help and protection. You can ask questions and learn
        about your options before deciding what feels right for you.
      </p>
      <%= link_to hotline_path, class: "btn btn-primary-custom mt-3" do %>
        Find support <i class="bi bi-arrow-right ms-2" aria-hidden="true"></i>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="resource-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="resource-section-heading">
        <span class="resource-eyebrow">POSSIBLE FIRST STEPS</span>
        <h2>Choose the route that feels safest.</h2>
        <p>There is no single right way to ask for help. If it is safe for you, you may:</p>
      </div>

      <div class="row g-4 mt-2">
        <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
          <article class="resource-card h-100">
            <span class="resource-step">01</span>
            <h3>Contact the police</h3>
            <p>
              For immediate danger, call <a href="tel:999">999</a>. To make a
              report, contact or visit a police station. You may ask about
              making a report in a language you understand.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
          <article class="resource-card h-100">
            <span class="resource-step">02</span>
            <h3>Ask JKM about protection</h3>
            <p>
              The Department of Social Welfare (JKM) can explain how to seek an
              Emergency Protection Order (EPO) and what support may be available.
              Talian Kasih can also guide callers to assistance.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
          <article class="resource-card h-100">
            <span class="resource-step">03</span>
            <h3>Seek medical care</h3>
            <p>
              If you are injured or need medical attention, go to a hospital or
              clinic. A government hospital's One Stop Crisis Centre (OSCC) may
              provide help for survivors of violence.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="resource-law-panel mt-5">
        <div class="resource-icon resource-icon-purple"><i class="bi bi-book-half" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
        <div>
          <span class="resource-eyebrow">THE LAW IN BRIEF</span>
          <h2>Domestic Violence Act 1994 (Act 521)</h2>
          <p>
            Malaysia's Domestic Violence Act provides for protection in
            specified circumstances and family relationships. Depending on
            the situation, protection may involve an Emergency Protection
            Order (EPO), Interim Protection Order (IPO), or Protection Order
            (PO). The process and eligibility differ; ask JKM, the police, or
            a qualified legal adviser about current requirements.
          </p>
          <p class="resource-disclaimer mb-0">
            This is general information, not legal advice. It does not replace
            guidance from the relevant authorities or a qualified adviser.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="resource-section resource-soft-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row g-5">
        <div class="col-lg-6">
          <span class="resource-eyebrow">IF YOU DECIDE TO MAKE A REPORT</span>
          <h2 class="resource-section-title mt-2">Share what you can, at your pace.</h2>
          <p class="resource-copy">
            You may describe what happened, when and where it happened, and
            whether anyone needs urgent medical care. If safe, keep copies of
            relevant messages, photographs, or medical records. Do not put
            yourself at risk to collect evidence.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-lg-6">
          <div class="resource-note">
            <i class="bi bi-heart-fill" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <p class="mb-0">
              You can ask a trusted person or support worker to accompany you.
              If an authority response does not feel clear, you can ask what
              the next step is or seek support from an advocate.
            </p>
          </div>
          <%= link_to "See support services and hotlines", hotline_path, class: "resource-link d-inline-block mt-4" %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
